<title>UK: BOE forecasts 2.3 bln stg shortage, offers help.</title>
<headline>BOE forecasts 2.3 bln stg shortage, offers help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England offered the UK money market a midday round of assistance after revising its forecast liquidity shortage to 2.3 billion stg, from an initial 2.4 billion.</p>
<p>The operations will comprise a repo to August 6 and outright offers of bills maturing on or before August 6.</p>
<p>It has already provided assistance totalling 1.267 billion stg on Thursday.</p>
